      "hints": [
        "Read each centre from standard circle form.",
        "Take the square root of each right-hand side.",
        "Use the distance formula between the centres."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$C_1$ has centre $(0,0)$ and radius $\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt5$.",
        "$C_2$ has centre $(12,16)$ and radius $\\sqrt{80}=4\\sqrt5$.",
        "The centre distance is $\\sqrt{12^2+16^2}=20$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_p1_t_coordinate_geometry_m06_l02_cpq07_p02",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p1_t_coordinate_geometry",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p1_t_coordinate_geometry_m06_l02"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Subtract the sum of the radii from the centre distance.",
        "Use Pythagoras on the vector components, then substitute $k$.",
        "Moving through the whole gap produces external contact."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "The gap is $20-(2\\sqrt5+4\\sqrt5)=20-6\\sqrt5$.",
        "The translation length is $\\sqrt{(3k)^2+(4k)^2}=5k=20-6\\sqrt5$.",
        "The translation equals the gap, so $C_3$ touches $C_2$ externally."
      ]
    }
  ]
